{%- comment -%}
  Full screen. Left column: halftone PSI map, its band legend, and the regional
  cities. Right column: the headline reading, pollutants, and the 24h forecast.
  Every variable used here is derived in shared.liquid, which TRMNL prepends
  to this file.

  Layout is framework classes throughout: a 12-column grid split 7/5 on the
  OG and 8/4 on the X (whose extra width goes to the map), and a single
  column in portrait. The OG rotated is only 480px wide and has no height
  to spare, so there the readings take two rows at a size down, the cities
  wrap to three across, and the per-region table stays X-only.

  The framework grid cannot reorder its cells, so the readings, which sit
  above the map in portrait, are emitted twice: beside the map, hidden in
  portrait, and above the grid, shown only in portrait. They are captured
  once, in shared.liquid, as headline_block, the pollutant bars and fc_block.
  The bars are the same five on every screen.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
  {%- if has_psi == false -%}
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--center h--full">
      <span class="title title--large">No air quality data</span>
      <span class="description">data.gov.sg did not return a PSI reading</span>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%} Portrait only: the readings as a row above the map. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="hidden portrait:block w--full">
      {%- comment -%}
        X: headline, bars and forecast three across. The OG is too narrow
        for that, so the bars sit beside the headline and the forecast takes
        a short row of its own underneath.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="grid grid--cols-2 lg:grid--cols-3">
        <div>{{ headline_block }}</div>
        <div>{{ pollutant_bars }}</div>
        <div class="col--span-2 lg:col--span-1 flex flex--col flex--stretch-x h--[70px] lg:h--full">{{ fc_block }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid--cols-12 w--full">

      <div class="col--span-7 lg:col--span-8 portrait:col--span-12 lg:portrait:col--span-12 flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--small">
        {{ map_svg }}

        {%- comment -%}
          The legend is the only thing that makes dot size readable as a
          number, so it sits directly under the map at the same dot sizes.
          Columns are spaced by band count, not a fixed step, because US AQI
          has six bands to PSI's five. Dot above label above boundary, all
          centred: setting the label beside its dot collides with the next
          dot once six columns have to fit. The scale's name is in the
          headline, so the row only needs its numbers.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign col_w = 430 | divided_by: band_count -%}
        {%- assign half_w = col_w | divided_by: 2 -%}
        <svg class="block value--tnums" viewBox="0 0 430 40" width="100%" font-family="Inter Variable, Inter, sans-serif" fill="currentColor">
          {%- for lbl in band_short -%}
            {%- assign cx = forloop.index0 | times: col_w | plus: half_w -%}
            <circle cx="{{ cx }}" cy="8" r="{{ band_radii[forloop.index0] }}"/>
            <text x="{{ cx }}" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="500">{{ lbl }}</text>
            {%- if forloop.first -%}
              {%- assign edge = 0 -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign prev = forloop.index0 | minus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign edge = band_edges[prev] | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            <text x="{{ cx }}" y="37" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700">{{ edge }}{% if forloop.last %}+{% endif %}</text>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </svg>

        <div class="border--h-5"></div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The X has height the OG does not, so it gets the per-region
          readings the map can only show as a dot size, and width for every
          pollutant NEA measures. The pollutants are PSI sub-indices, the
          figures the bars show for the home region: one scale across the
          columns, where NEA's concentrations mix ug/m3 with whole-number
          mg/m3 (CO reads 1 almost everywhere). No caption to say so: the
          X's full height has no line to spare, and the bars beside or above
          carry the "PSI sub-index" heading.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="hidden lg:block">
          <div class="grid grid--cols-7">
            <span class="label label--small">Region</span>
            <span class="label label--small">{{ scale_short }}</span>
            <span class="label label--small">PM2.5</span>
            <span class="label label--small">PM10</span>
            <span class="label label--small">Ozone</span>
            <span class="label label--small">SO2</span>
            <span class="label label--small">CO</span>
          </div>
          <div class="border--h-5"></div>
          {%- for layer in map_layers -%}
            {%- assign rname = layer | split: '|' | first -%}
            <div class="grid grid--cols-7">
              <span class="title title--small">{{ rname | capitalize }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ region_values[forloop.index0] }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ readings.pm25_sub_index[rname] | default: '–' }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ readings.pm10_sub_index[rname] | default: '–' }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ readings.o3_sub_index[rname] | default: '–' }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ readings.so2_sub_index[rname] | default: '–' }}</span>
              <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ readings.co_sub_index[rname] | default: '–' }}</span>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <div>{{ city_strip }}</div>
      </div>

      <div class="col--span-5 lg:col--span-4 portrait:hidden flex--col flex--stretch-x flex--center-y gap--small lg:gap--distribute">
        {{ headline_block }}
        <div class="border--h-5"></div>
        {%- comment -%} The OG's column has no height for the stacked bars; the X's does. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div>
          <div class="lg:hidden">{{ pollutant_bars_inline }}</div>
          <div class="hidden lg:block">{{ pollutant_bars }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="border--h-5"></div>
        <div>{{ fc_block }}</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- render 'title_bar', icon: title_icon, instance: nea_stamp -%}
